  "source": "Warhammer: The Game of Fantasy Battles - 9th Edition v3.11, Troop Types chapter (p71-76)",
  "notes": [
    "Hand-maintained. The Troop Types chapter is prose, not a ruled table, so extract_core_rules.py cannot lift these figures — core-rules.json carries only the descriptive text.",
    "Divergences from wap-v2: Monstrous Infantry and Monstrous Beasts support three attacks rather than two; mounts may not make supporting attacks at all; Cavalry without a split profile drops from two to one; Cavalry and Monstrous Cavalry lose their inherent Impact Hits; no troop type grants Swiftstride any more (Independent took its place, which has no combat effect here).",
    "large-infantry is not a wap-v3 troop type — the chapter drops it, and the nine wap-v2 units that declared it were re-typed. One wap-v3 entry still names it (Zoggrok Anvilsmasha, Orcs & Goblins), so the row is kept rather than letting a lookup throw. Figures carried over from wap-v2."
  ],
